// The viewport's width in pixels, which is what the lens is derived from. Its own
// file because a file holds three functions and d3_viewport needs all three of
// its neighbours.

d3_vp_w() {
  int ret_i = (import d3_vp)[2] - (import d3_vp)[0] + 1;
} return int ret_i;
given d3_t_setup ():(64)
given d3_t_vp_odd_setup ():(10)

// d3_vp[4], the viewport's centre x -- read by cases that mutate d3_vp_mid's
// input rect but have no other way to observe slot 4 from outside.
d3_t_vp_cx() {
  int cx = (import d3_vp)[4];
} return int cx;
given d3_t_setup ():(32)
given d3_t_vp_odd_setup ():(8)

// A camera moved off the origin and given a wide-ish fov, for cases in the
// cam/mat batch that need a non-zero eye or a re-derived focal length without
// disturbing the aim. The eye change and the fov change are independent
// slots, so one setup covers both a d3_view_eye case and a d3_cam_focal/
// d3_start case.
d3_t_fixture2() {
  d3_t_setup();
  d3_cam_set(500, 0 - 300, 1200);
  d3_cam_fov(90000);
} return void;
():() then d3_t_cam:([500, -300, 1200, 0, 0, 40, 40000, 90000, 32000])
():() then d3_vp_w:(64)
